/*
 * data.js — PSERS portfolio data & slide catalogue
 * ----------------------------------------------------------------------
 * Everything in this file is DATA, not logic (see app.js for behavior).
 * It defines the single global `CFG` object that app.js reads from.
 *
 * Source of truth: CFG.rows and CFG.totalNav below (between the GENERATED
 * sentinel comments) are produced by tools/export_cfg_rows.py from the
 * same Excel pipeline (psers_data_pipeline.py, reading "PSERS_Total
 * Private Market Portfolio_Final.xlsx", sheet "Clean Data") that every
 * migrated slide already uses — the same 363 Include rows as Key
 * Considerations / Strategy Mix / Portfolio Holdings, not the old 368-row
 * hand-carried-over-from-v6 dataset those pages and this file's popups
 * used to disagree on (Round 73). Do not hand-edit the rows array; re-run
 * `python3 tools/export.py` after the source workbook changes. See
 * README.md's "Data pipeline" section.
 *
 * CFG.rows field reference (each element is one fund/investment interest):
 *   investment          Investment Name
 *   portfolio           Portfolio Name (Tangible's top-level bucket)
 *   asset                Asset Name
 *   manager              Manager Name (GP)
 *   vehicle              Vehicle Type (e.g. Commingled Fund, Co-Investment)
 *   vintage              Vintage year
 *   strategy / strategy2 Legacy 6-way taxonomy (Buyout/Real Estate/Credit/
 *                        Infrastructure/Growth & Venture/Special Situations),
 *                        derived from tier1 — NOT the same field as the
 *                        Strategy Mix slide's coarser "strategy" label.
 *                        strategy2 duplicates strategy (dead field, kept for
 *                        schema completeness — see export_cfg_rows.py docstring).
 *   tier1 / tier2 / tier3  Asset Class Tier 1-3 (Investment)
 *   commitment           Original commitment ($)
 *   nav                  Net Asset Value / latest valuation ($)
 *   dist                 Total distributions ($)
 *   paid                 Total paid-in capital ($)
 *   unfunded             Unfunded commitment ($)
 *   commitment_revised   Paid + unfunded
 *   total_value          dist + nav
 *   funded_pct           paid / (paid + unfunded)
 *   unfunded_pct         unfunded / commitment, capped at 1; 0 if commitment is 0
 *   dpi                  Distributions to Paid-In = dist / paid
 *   rvpi                 Residual Value to Paid-In = nav / paid
 *   tvpi                 Total Value to Paid-In = total_value / paid
 *   vintage_segment      Bucketed vintage band used for the vintage chart
 *   unfunded_segment     Bucketed unfunded-% band
 *   dpi_segment          Bucketed DPI band ("Under 0.25x" / "0.25x-0.75x" / "Over 0.75x") —
 *                        drives the manager-concentration chart's 3 columns
 *   tvpi_segment         Bucketed TVPI band
 *   nav_segment          Bucketed NAV-size band
 *
 * To update the numbers: edit the source Excel, then run
 * `python3 tools/export.py` (or just tools/export_cfg_rows.py) — it
 * re-derives CFG.rows/CFG.totalNav from the pipeline and splices the
 * result back in between the GENERATED sentinel comments below. Do not
 * hand-edit the array itself.
 *
 * CFG.titles: deck order. Nav-dot count is this array's length.
 * Every title must have a matching HTML_SLIDES entry in app.js.
 * The deck is HTML-only — there is no slide-image fallback.
 *
 * CFG.totalNav: total portfolio NAV across ALL rows, used to compute the
 * "% of portfolio" figures shown throughout the drill-down drawers.
 */


